Subject: [PATCH 43/46] doc: the gpiomem load's limits, exits that leave pins
 driven, the rate assumption

The Lattice page now says: a compatible that exists but cannot be read stops
the load; an output at the start is refused; the GPFSEL read-modify-write
can lose another writer's update to a neighbouring pin; which exits put the
pins back (error, SIGINT, SIGTERM, SIGHUP, SIGQUIT, SIGPIPE) and which leave
them driven (SIGKILL, crashes, abort, terminate, exit) and how to recover;
how the pad is calibrated and scaled to the CPU's maximum and minimum clock;
and the assumption (posted writes) that the hardware trial measures. "at or
under 20 MHz", and the long lines wrapped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JG8Wtod8kFmcquwN34pFCa
